# Lumen: the cluster stack ships installed and OFF.
#
# A node that is not in a cluster must not start half of one at boot — a
# corosync with no configuration flaps, and a pacemaker with no corosync
# fails. The cluster-create and node-add workflows are the only things that
# enable these (systemctl enable --now, per member), and cluster destroy
# disables them again. The preset records that default so a fresh install
# and an upgrade agree.
#
# pcsd stays off for a stronger reason: Lumen deliberately does not use
# `pcs cluster setup`, so nothing ever needs the daemon or its hacluster
# account — see docs/cluster.md, "pcs configures; it does not install".
disable corosync.service
disable pacemaker.service
disable pcsd.service
